## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Work Manager Next.js project.

### What Was Implemented

1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**: Retrieved the most up-to-date installation instructions from the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)

2. **Identified Framework**: Confirmed the project uses Next.js with App Router architecture (based on the presence of `app/layout.tsx`)

3. **Installed Package**: Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to the project dependencies using npm

4. **Added Analytics Component**: Implemented the Analytics component in the root layout file following Next.js App Router best practices:
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag in `app/layout.tsx`

### Files Modified

- **frontend/app/layout.tsx**: Added Analytics import and component
- **frontend/package.json**: Added `@vercel/analytics` dependency
- **frontend/package-lock.json**: Updated with new dependency tree

### Implementation Details

The Analytics component was placed inside the `<body>` tag, after the `<ThemeProvider>` component, following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router. This ensures analytics tracking is enabled across all pages of the application.

The implementation preserves all existing functionality including:
- Custom fonts (Fraunces, Inter, JetBrains Mono)
- Theme provider context
- Theme initialization script
- All existing metadata and styling

### Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (no TypeScript errors)
- ✅ Project compiles without issues
- ✅ Linter ran (pre-existing warnings unrelated to Analytics changes)
- ✅ No test script configured in package.json
- ✅ Lock file properly updated

### Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics tracking in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard → Analytics section
3. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics for the project
4. Verify tracking by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view` after deployment

The analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals once the feature is enabled in the Vercel dashboard.
